摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"DeepSeek Harness Desktop — A native desktop app for DeepSeek Harness (dsh). Open the app and start using the agent harness immediately — no terminal, no browser, no setup","id":"gh:1333280320","install_available":false,"language":"JavaScript","name":"deepseek-harness-app","slug":"zneoxlab/deepseek-harness-app","topics":["dsh","dsh-plugin","dsh-plugins"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"DeepSeek Harness Desktop — A native desktop app for DeepSeek Harness (dsh). Open the app and start u"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"sing the agent harness immediately — no terminal, no browser, no setup"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"DeepSeek Harness App"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"Cross-platform desktop client for DeepSeek Harness\nA native shell around the official dsh web UI — f"},{"id":"p3s2","text":"used title bar, tray residency, and a settings page with update management (short: dsh-app)"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"English ·\n中文"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> **DeepSeek Harness App (dsh-app) is not an official DeepSeek product.** It wraps the loc"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"al DeepSeek Harness (`dsh`) CLI into a desktop app: it automatically detects your Node/npm/dsh envir"},{"id":"p5s3","text":"onment, installs or upgrades missing pieces with one click, starts/reuses a plugin-enabled `dsh web`"},{"id":"p5s4","text":" when the app launches, and gives the official web UI the desktop experience it deserves — a fused t"},{"id":"p5s5","text":"itle bar, tray residency, notifications, autostart, global shortcuts and connect modes."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"## Why not a full rewrite?"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"The official `dsh` ships a **complete web UI** (sessions, projects, permissions, skills, plugins, me"},{"id":"p7s2","text":"dia — everything lives there). The official ACP server (`@deepseek-ai/dsh-acp`) is automation-only: "},{"id":"p7s3","text":"it creates fresh sessions but cannot load / list / resume / fork existing ones, so it cannot power a"},{"id":"p7s4","text":" full desktop console."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"That is why **DeepSeek Harness App builds on the official web UI instead of reinventing it**: we add"},{"id":"p8s2","text":" only what a browser cannot — a native shell, tray residency, and desktop integrations."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"## Why this is different from fork-based shells"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"Some desktop clients fork or vendor the DeepSeek Harness source and ship their own “core”. That make"},{"id":"p10s2","text":"s the package heavier, can drift from upstream, and often freezes the core until the shell project u"},{"id":"p10s3","text":"pdates it. dsh-app does the opposite:"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"|  | Fork/vendor-based shells | dsh-app |"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"| **Core** | Bundle or fork the dsh codebase, often with modified internals | Use the official local"},{"id":"p12s2","text":" `@deepseek-ai/dsh` CLI from npm — no fork, no rewrite |\n| **Update path** | Wait for the shell main"},{"id":"p12s3","text":"tainer to merge upstream changes | Sync official dsh releases from npm/GitHub Releases; one-click ch"},{"id":"p12s4","text":"eck and upgrade |\n| **Independence** | If the shell stops being maintained, the bundled core can be "},{"id":"p12s5","text":"stuck | dsh core is official and can always be upgraded independently of this App |\n| **Footprint** "},{"id":"p12s6","text":"| Often Electron + copied/duplicated web UI | Lightweight Tauri native shell + official web UI; dsh "},{"id":"p12s7","text":"runs from your local installation |\n| **Browser access** | The shell may own/alter the only running "},{"id":"p12s8","text":"server or fork the UI | App starts or reuses the standard local dsh web — the same service stays rea"},{"id":"p12s9","text":"chable in your browser |"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"Practical highlights:"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"- **Automatic Node / CLI detection** — the startup wizard checks Node, npm, and dsh in order; it fin"},{"id":"p14s2","text":"ds dsh from `DSH_BIN` → npm global → PATH → common install dirs, and reports versions and paths.\n- *"},{"id":"p14s3","text":"*One-click install / upgrade** — missing Node? The app downloads an official managed Node into `~/.d"},{"id":"p14s4","text":"sh-app/node` (no admin). Missing dsh? It installs `@deepseek-ai/dsh` through npm automatically (mirr"},{"id":"p14s5","text":"or-aware in Chinese environments). Both App and dsh CLI can be checked and upgraded from the setting"},{"id":"p14s6","text":"s page.\n- **Automatic start/stop management** — on launch the App reuses a bridge-enabled `dsh web` "},{"id":"p14s7","text":"at `127.0.0.1:3080`, or starts its own `dsh --profile dsh-app --port 0`; on quit it cleans up the wh"},{"id":"p14s8","text":"ole process tree. Your manually started plain `dsh web` is left untouched, and launching the App doe"},{"id":"p14s9","text":"s not block browser access.\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"## Contents"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"1. Why this is different from fork-based shells\n2. Features\n3. Screenshots\n4. How it connects\n5. Ins"},{"id":"p16s2","text":"tall\n6. First run & troubleshooting\n7. Develop & build\n8. Testing failure scenarios\n9. Project struc"},{"id":"p16s3","text":"ture\n10. Roadmap\n11. License"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"## Features"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"| Area | What you get |"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"| **Smart connect** | Detects `dsh` CLI (DSH_BIN → npm global → PATH → common install dirs); reuses "},{"id":"p19s2","text":"a running **bridge-enabled** instance on `127.0.0.1:3080`, otherwise starts its own `dsh --profile d"},{"id":"p19s3","text":"sh-app --port 0` on a free random port (a plain `dsh web` you started manually is left alone) |\n| **"},{"id":"p19s4","text":"Node / CLI auto detection** | Startup wizard checks Node, npm, and dsh step by step, reports version"},{"id":"p19s5","text":"s/paths, and warns when the managed Node is too old |\n| **dsh CLI detection** | Startup wizard when "},{"id":"p19s6","text":"the CLI is missing — copy the install command, one-click install/upgrade, re-check with one click |\n"},{"id":"p19s7","text":"| **One-click environment install** | Missing Node or dsh? Install them inside the app: official man"},{"id":"p19s8","text":"aged Node to `~/.dsh-app/node`, then `@deepseek-ai/dsh` via npm global (mirror-aware, no admin requi"},{"id":"p19s9","text":"red) |\n| **Fused title bar** | A borderless window with a title bar fused into the system frame, per"},{"id":"p19s10","text":"-platform window buttons: **macOS** uses the native title bar entirely (real system traffic lights, "},{"id":"p19s11","text":"native rounded corners and shadow); **Windows** draws Win11-style square caption buttons at the top-"},{"id":"p19s12","text":"right; **Linux** draws neutral circle buttons at the top-left. Windows 11 rounds the whole window au"},{"id":"p19s13","text":"tomatically (undecorated + shadow). The strip is the drag region; double-click maximizes. Title bar "},{"id":"p19s14","text":"colors follow the **in-app theme** (dark / light / system) on every platform |\n| **Sidebar status ro"},{"id":"p19s15","text":"w (bottom-left)** | A status capsule (**colored dot + 已连接 / 未连接**) at the very bottom-left of the si"},{"id":"p19s16","text":"debar **below the settings button**, app version on the right; hover shows dsh CLI version and servi"},{"id":"p19s17","text":"ce URL, click copies the connection info (registered through the official `sidebar.footer.action` sl"},{"id":"p19s18","text":"ot; the settings row moves up one slot) |\n| **DSH App settings page** | A page registered into the o"},{"id":"p19s19","text":"fficial settings panel: app info (version, source-code link) + **update management against GitHub Re"},{"id":"p19s20","text":"leases**; dsh CLI info (version / source / service URL) + **CLI version management** (latest check a"},{"id":"p19s21","text":"gainst the npm registry, one-click update, copy update command) |\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"## Screenshots"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"> From the current Windows development build."},{"id":"p22s1","text":"| Startup — detecting CLI | dsh CLI missing — install wizard |\n|:---:|:---:|"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"| Home — official dsh web UI inside the shell |\n|:---:|"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"| DSH App settings page — app + dsh CLI update management | Sidebar bottom-left status row — connect"},{"id":"p24s2","text":"ion status & info |\n|:---:|:---:|"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"## How it connects"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"## Install"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"### 1. Get the app"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"Download the installer for your platform from Releases (Windows NSIS, macOS DMG, Linux AppImage/deb "},{"id":"p30s2","text":"— coming as builds are published)."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
